In './MMS/build_3D_VDF.py':
    MT added a self.angular basis to setup_rec_grid so that G_interp can be calculated for both the Slepian and Spherical Harmonic codes.
    before: G_interp[Slep_idx] = interpolate.griddata(points, vdf_rec_dict.G[:,:,Slep_idx].flatten(), (pp, tt))
    after: G_interp[Slep_idx] = interpolate.griddata(points, vdf_rec_dict.G[Slep_idx].flatten(), (pp, tt))



In 'reconstruct_VDF.py':
    I changed the code such that the Slepian coefficients were generated only at one time. In the previous implementation, at each time_idx
    the code was generating the Slepian basis functions on the same angular extent. Perhaps this is the correct implementation, however, this 
    resulted in a run time of roughly 4 hrs and 30 mins approximately.

In 'source_scripts/setup_rec_grid.py':
    I added to the MMS class the angular basis keyword. We now pass the angular basis ensuring that the choice of Spherical Harmonics or Slepians 
    is included. This will be used in multiple places throughout the code.

